tasks.description:
Bug: `startNarrationServer()` in `src/narration.ts` waits 1s then does a single health check. Kokoro TTS takes 3-5s to init, so the check fires too early and throws.

Fix (TDD — write tests first):

1. In `test/narration.test.ts`, add tests for:
   - Retry succeeds on Nth attempt (mock `checkNarrationHealth` to return false N-1 times then true)
   - Early exit on first success (verify health check is not called more than necessary)
   - Throws after all retries exhausted (mock health check to always return false)

2. In `src/narration.ts` `startNarrationServer()`, replace:
   ```ts
   await new Promise<void>((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 1000));
   const healthy = await checkNarrationHealth(socketPath);
   if (!healthy) {
     throw new Error('Narration server failed health check after startup');
   }
   ```
   With a retry loop: poll `checkNarrationHealth()` up to 10 times with 1s intervals (~10s max wait). Return PID on first successful PONG. Throw only if all 10 retries are exhausted.

3. Run `bun test test/narration.test.ts` to confirm all tests pass.
